    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23sZmuL1MsmYTfmFAfbKUto)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Independent; touches only `init.el` (one `sp-load` line), a new module, its doc, a test and a README row.\n\n## What and why\n- MELPA renamed its default branch `master` → `main`; Elpaca's `elpaca-menu-melpa` still hardcodes `master`, so `elpaca-update-menus` fails (\"Unable to clone MELPA\").\n- Upstream: [elpaca #585](https://github.com/progfolio/elpaca/issues/585), [PR #586](https://github.com/progfolio/elpaca/pull/586) (both still open).\n- New module `sp-elpaca-melpa-fix` advises `elpaca-menu-melpa--clone` / `--update` to use `main`, instead of editing Elpaca's sources.\n- Loaded from `init.el` right after the Elpaca bootstrap, before the first `elpaca` call.\n\n## Temporary by design\n- `sp-elpaca-melpa-fix` (defcustom, default t) switches it off; `sp-elpaca-melpa-branch` (default \"main\") sets the branch.\n- Disables itself when Elpaca defines `elpaca-melpa-branch` (what PR 586 adds).\n- Remove: delete the `sp-load` line in `init.el`, the `.el`, the `.org` doc, the test and the README row.\n\n## Differences from upstream PR 586\n- Update does `git fetch --depth=1 origin main` + `git checkout -B main FETCH_HEAD` rather than `git pull origin main`, so an existing cache still on `master` is repaired in place (no manual deletion of `var/elpaca/cache/melpa`).\n- I could only read a summary of PR 586's diff plus the current upstream `elpaca-menu-melpa.el`; I wrote the code from that, not by copying the PR.\n\n## Verified here (Emacs 29.3, container)\n- Module byte-compiles with no warnings; tangles from the literate doc.\n- 3 ERT tests pass (`tests/sp-elpaca-melpa-fix-test.el`): clone commands use `main` and never `master`; inactive paths call the originals; update moves a real local checkout from `master` (remote renamed to `main`) onto the new `main` commit.\n\n## Not verified\n- Not run against a real Elpaca or the real MELPA repo (no network to MELPA recipes, Elpaca not installed).\n- Not tried on macOS / with Emacs 31 / on your real `var/elpaca` cache.\n- The advice running early enough in `init.el` is by reasoning only.\n- Branch is not number-prefixed: the cloud session may only push to its assigned branch.\n\n## Manual testing checklist\n- [x] Start Emacs with the PR checked out; no errors in `*Messages*` or `*elpaca-log*`.\n- [x] `M-x elpaca-update-menus` finishes; `*Messages*` shows \"Downloading MELPA...100%\".\n- [ ] In `var/elpaca/cache/melpa/`, `git branch` shows `main` tracking `origin/main`.\n- [ ] `M-x elpaca-try` a MELPA-only package installs.\n- [ ] `M-x elpaca-update-all` (or `elpaca-pull` on a MELPA package) works.\n- [ ] Fresh clone: move `var/elpaca/cache/melpa` aside, run `elpaca-update-menus`; it re-clones.\n- [ ] Set `sp-elpaca-melpa-fix` to nil: Elpaca's original (broken) behaviour returns, confirming the switch.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9x8iU8uUb42qXRcTV)_",
